## Summary
Texas A&M University Victoria has implemented a policy requiring faculty to be on campus five days a week, leading to several resignations. This policy is in response to a new Texas law that restricts remote work for public university faculty. The Texas AAUP has reported that the change has caused significant chaos and emotional distress among staff.

## Key Points
- Texas A&M University Victoria mandated a five-day on-campus requirement for faculty.
- Several faculty members have quit due to the new policy.
- The policy is a direct response to a Texas law limiting remote work for public university faculty.
- The Texas AAUP has criticized the policy for causing chaos and tears among faculty.


